Note on E4 (question M24065e66c77fea00): the record populates `change_value: -760` / `change_unit: m_usd` even though this is exactly `level (13540) - comparison (14300)` — a closed shape (point vs point). Per the NUMBERS rule ("Leave change_value null when it could merely be derived from a closed shape; derive at read time"), this should have been left null, as correctly done in the analogous PRASM (E1) and CASM (E2) records where an explicitly-stated, equally-derivable percent change was properly omitted. That is the basis for marking `record_matches_source` false there.